    "slot_key": "Dataset eligibility rules for visualization",
    "slot_value": "Tabular experimental results and sample measurements that can be mapped onto a grid; annotated biological records are also supported if they include identifiers and related metadata that can be displayed when a point is selected. Records that can’t be placed meaningfully on the grid should be excluded from the 3D view, grouped separately, or flagged as incomplete; anything without enough identifier or metadata detail should not appear as a selectable point unless there is at least some useful summary attached. The practical rule is whether the user can still learn something useful from it: if there is enough information to identify it and show a meaningful summary, keep it as a placeholder; if it is too incomplete to support any real inspection, exclude it from the main grid and list it separately as incomplete. When upstream data is partial, the inspection view should show it with clear completeness limits rather than silently omitting it, keep available fields visible, label what is missing, and summarize it as incomplete if it is too sparse to be useful. The application must stay responsive even with large datasets, and grouping/comparison should not make the view sluggish.",
